# --- Retired routes (moved here 2026-08-09) -------------------------------
# These were Astro.redirect() stubs. In a STATIC build that does not emit an
# HTTP 301 — Astro writes an HTML file carrying a meta-refresh and
# <meta name="robots" content="noindex">. Search Console therefore filed them
# under "Excluded by 'noindex' tag" rather than "Page with redirect", and the
# link equity pointing at the old URLs went nowhere.
#
# A real 301 at the edge fixes all three: correct reporting, equity passed to
# the target, and no HTML round-trip.
#
# ⚠️ The .astro stubs MUST stay deleted. Cloudflare Pages serves a matching
# static file in preference to a _redirects rule, so leaving dist/tiers.html
# in place would silently shadow the rule below and nothing would change.
/tiers                              /rates                    301
/intelligence                       /research                 301
/vision                             /applications             301
/availability                       /utilization              301
/research/rent-and-launch-price     /research/rent-and-msrp   301
/research/unfinancialized-compute   /credit                   301

